# The agent acceptance test §12 asks for: a new spell, verified by its author
# without reading a state dump by eye.
#
# `Glacier Lance` is bolt + frost, added to scripts/spellbook.lua with a sprite
# imported alongside it. This asserts the spell exists, fires, and kills.

# The evolution is registered and the trial found it.
tick 10 /Arena01 var:spell_name == Glacier Lance
# There used to be a `var:missing != true` here. It passed because the field
# was not there at all, which is no longer how a probe behaves. The name above
# is the assertion that was doing the work.

# It fires.
tick 60 /Arena01 var:fired > 0

# And it damages what it hits: a skeleton has 40 health and the Lance does 38,
# so two hits kill it.
tick 120 /Arena01 var:target_health < 40
tick 199 /Arena01 var:target_alive == false
